### Task 4 — Validity Audit

| Threat | Description | Control / Disclosure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hardware Heterogeneity** | The CPU and GPU may have different memory bandwidths or thermal throttling profiles. | Use the same machine for all tests; disclose thermal state/throttling logs. |
| **Software/Driver Overhead** | CUDA, Vulkan, and CPU backends use different libraries (cuBLAS vs. rocBLAS vs. OpenBLAS). | Use identical model weights and identical precision across all backends. |
| **Workload Comparability** | The prompt length or generation length might vary between runs, affecting throughput. | **Strictly enforce identical input tokens and identical max-generation tokens for every test.** |
| **Statistical Insignificance** | Three runs are a very small sample size for stochastic or thermally sensitive processes. | Report the Standard Deviation/Variance and disclose the small sample size ($N=3$). |

